---
import Analytics from "../../components/Analytics.astro";

const TITLE = "PG&E Rate Hike Audit 2026: Solar & Battery Protection Analysis";
const DESCRIPTION = "Analysis of Pacific Gas & Electric (PG&E) electricity rate increases and how home battery storage offsets E-ELEC peak pricing.";
const CANONICAL_URL = "https://mygridpermit.com/blog/pge-rate-hikes-2026/";
const HEADLINE = "PG&E Rate Hikes in 2026: Impact Analysis for Northern California Solar Owners";

// No datePublished/dateModified/image: the page's own visible text only
// states "Updated July 2026" (month precision), and no real hero image
// asset exists for this post — adding either here would assert more
// precision/content than we actually have.
const articleSchema = {
	"@context": "https://schema.org",
	"@type": "Article",
	headline: HEADLINE,
	description: DESCRIPTION,
	mainEntityOfPage: { "@type": "WebPage", "@id": CANONICAL_URL },
	author: { "@type": "Organization", name: "GridPermit" },
	publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "GridPermit" },
};
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
	<Analytics />
	<meta charset="UTF-8">
	<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
	<title>{TITLE}</title>
	<meta name="description" content={DESCRIPTION} />
	<link rel="canonical" href={CANONICAL_URL} />
	<meta property="og:type" content="article" />
	<meta property="og:url" content={CANONICAL_URL} />
	<meta property="og:title" content={TITLE} />
	<meta property="og:description" content={DESCRIPTION} />
	<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary" />
	<meta name="twitter:title" content={TITLE} />
	<meta name="twitter:description" content={DESCRIPTION} />
	<meta name="google-site-verification" content="b36wwqlXise5bGI8ckWqbybnEoCYlsTmp4BiV" />
	<link rel="sitemap" href="/sitemap-index.xml" />
	<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
	<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
	<link rel="preload" as="style" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Plus+Jakarta+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700;800&display=swap" class="async-font-css">
	<noscript><link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Plus+Jakarta+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700;800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet"></noscript>
	<script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(articleSchema)} />
</head>
<body data-track-view="blog_article_viewed">
	<nav class="navbar"><div class="nav-container"><a href="/" class="brand-logo">Grid<strong>Permit</strong></a><div class="nav-links"><a href="/blog">Blog</a><a href="/california/solar-permit-guides/">California Guides</a><a href="/methodology">Methodology</a><a href="/search">Search</a></div><a href="/#calculator" class="btn-cta-nav">Run Free ROI Audit</a></div></nav>
	<main class="article-container">
		<span class="article-category">Utility Rate Audit</span>
		<h1>{HEADLINE}</h1>
		<p class="article-meta">Updated July 2026 • 7 min read</p>
		
		<p class="lead-paragraph">Pacific Gas & Electric (PG&E) electricity rates have increased significantly over the past three years. For Northern California homeowners, rising baseline delivery costs make utility bill management a top financial priority.</p>

		<h2>1. PG&E Rate Escalation Trends</h2>
		<p>According to CPUC filings, average PG&E residential rates increased over 35% between 2021 and 2026, driven by grid undergrounding projects, wildfire mitigation investments, and capacity upgrades. Peak summer rates under TOU-C schedule now routinely exceed $0.55/kWh.</p>

		<h2>2. Impact on NEM 3.0 Solar Owners</h2>
		<p>PG&E customers installing solar under NEM 3.0 are automatically placed on rate schedules like E-ELEC. Because midday export values remain low (~$0.05/kWh), solar-only systems leave homeowners vulnerable to high evening peak charges when returning home from work.</p>

		<h2>3. Mitigation Strategy: Battery Peak Shaving</h2>
		<p>By pairing solar panels with a 10–15 kWh battery storage unit, homeowners isolate themselves from PG&E's highest pricing tiers. The battery powers the home from 4 PM to 9 PM, discharging clean energy generated earlier in the day.</p>

		<h2>4. Sources & Methodology</h2>
		<p class="sources-text"><strong>Sources:</strong> PG&E Advice Letter filings with CPUC; Rate Schedule E-ELEC and TOU-C tariff sheets; CPUC Energy Division rate tracker reports (2026). <em>Figures above are illustrative examples based on publicly reported rate ranges, not a live lookup of your bill — confirm current rates with PG&E before making a decision.</em></p>

		<p>Looking for your city's specific solar permit requirements rather than rate analysis? See our <a href="/california/utility/pg-e/">verified PG&E city guides</a>.</p>

		<div class="cta-banner">
			<h3>Check Your Estimated PG&E Bill Offset</h3>
			<a href="/#calculator" class="btn-banner-cta">Run Free ROI Calculator →</a>
		</div>
	</main>
	<footer class="footer"><p>© 2026 GridPermit. All rights reserved.</p><p class="footer-links"><a href="/blog">Blog</a> · <a href="/california/solar-permit-guides/">California Guides</a> · <a href="/methodology">Methodology</a> · <a href="/">Home</a></p></footer>
	<style>
		:root { --primary: #2563eb; --bg-slate: #f8fafc; --text-main: #0f172a; }
		body { font-family: 'Plus Jakarta Sans', system-ui, sans-serif; background: var(--bg-slate); color: var(--text-main); line-height: 1.7; margin: 0; }
		.navbar { background: white; border-bottom: 1px solid #e2e8f0; padding: 1rem 2rem; }
		.nav-container { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; }
		.nav-links { display: flex; gap: 1.1rem; }
		.nav-links a { color: #64748b; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.85rem; }
		.nav-container { max-width: 1000px; margin: 0 auto; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; }
		.brand-logo { text-decoration: none; font-size: 1.5rem; color: #0f172a; }
		.btn-cta-nav { background: var(--primary); color: white; padding: 0.5rem 1rem; border-radius: 6px; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.85rem; }
		@media (max-width: 640px) {
			.nav-container { flex-wrap: wrap; row-gap: 0.6rem; }
			.nav-links { flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center; }
		}
		.article-container { max-width: 820px; margin: 3rem auto; padding: 0 1.5rem; }
		.article-category { font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 800; color: var(--primary); text-transform: uppercase; }
		h1 { font-size: 2.25rem; font-weight: 800; margin: 0.5rem 0; line-height: 1.25; }
		.article-meta { font-size: 0.85rem; color: #64748b; margin-bottom: 2rem; }
		.lead-paragraph { font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 500; color: #334155; }
		h2 { font-size: 1.4rem; font-weight: 800; margin-top: 2rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
		p { margin-bottom: 1rem; color: #334155; }
		.sources-text { font-size: 0.82rem; color: #64748b; background: #e2e8f0; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 8px; margin-top: 2rem; line-height: 1.5; }
		.cta-banner { background: #0f172a; color: white; padding: 2.5rem; border-radius: 12px; text-align: center; margin-top: 3rem; }
		.btn-banner-cta { background: #10b981; color: white; padding: 0.85rem 1.75rem; border-radius: 8px; font-weight: 800; text-decoration: none; display: inline-block; margin-top: 1rem; }
		.footer { text-align: center; padding: 2rem; color: #64748b; font-size: 0.85rem; }
		.footer-links { margin-top: 0.5rem; }
		.footer-links a { color: #64748b; text-decoration: none; }
	</style>
</body>
</html>
